		<!-- Puffin Notes. The reasons I have all of the Turrets have cloaking are first, Chris mentioned the idea of cloaking Turrets in a forum post a long, long time ago, Era of Discovery I think, and I remembered it.
		     It was something that never occurred en masse in player hands, but it has some use here.
			 First is theme. Neinzul, outside of the timed life Younglings and such, are rather underhanded. This can be seen in Classic, what with their Champion being the cloaked one, with reclamation weapons, weapons with damage to near death units, etc.
			 So I wish to carry that here.
			 Second is to assist with the operation of the Turrets. The notes on how this works will be next to the Turret in question, as they all have a different interaction with it. !-->
		
		
       <!-- Wormhole only Turret. Hybrid of Ambush and Deathgrip. Cloaking is to keep it alive as it does its initial burst of damage (as such Turrets are sitting in the alpha strike area) to the things held in tractors from the Array further below.
            The fact these have such high burst damage, particularly to things also in tractor beams, means they sort of clear out what an Array was holding, so the Array can in a way snare more targets than it seems.	   !-->		
		
		
